{"topic": "science", "claim": "The 32-year-old plasterer was shot and killed by excise officer Francis Smith, who mistook him for the Hammersmith ghost due to his white uniform. Smith was later sentenced to death, but his sentence was commuted to one year's imprisonment with hard labor, and he received a full pardon later in the year.", "sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_unusual_deaths_in_the_19th_century"], "image_hint": "", "quirky_score": 2, "discovered_at": "2026-05-03T19:31:01.981812Z", "source_kind": "wikipedia:unusual_deaths", "reddit_id": "wiki:ud:389496251687", "upvotes": 0, "verified_by": "auto:multi_check"}
